    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d636">

                <pb facs="0958" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/221</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Elihu Root, of the American Delegation at the
                        Conference on the Limitation of Armament, to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Regarding the proposal
                    that Rogers<anchor n="11" xml:id="d636-f1"/> should join with the British,
                    French and Japanese experts on electrical communications: In conferring
                    informally and quite outside of the Conference— <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>With a view to bringing about an understanding between the private
                            interests now holding monopolies or preferential privileges in China to
                            the end that friction may be prevented and the monopolies or
                            preferential privileges be so far as possible abrogated through friendly
                            agreement; and</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>With a view to recommending proposals for the improvement of
                            Trans-Pacific communication services, particularly with reference to
                            press messages—</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>With the understanding that any recommendations are to be reported to the foreign
                    offices concerned and not to this Conference, <pb facs="0959" n="839"
                        xml:id="pg839"/> I think such a conference is very desirable and Mr. Rogers
                    may well take part in it.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d636-f1" n="11" xml:id="d636-f1-content">
                <p>Walter S. Rogers, technical expert for communications to the American Delegation
                    at the Conference on the Limitation of Armament.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
